Consider the “root elements” of $U twisted(2, F_4)(K)$, cf. Section
@sec:l2012-extremal-en-preliminaries. Let $r = q_(i j)$. Put
$R_(i j)(t) = x_r lr((t)) x_(overline(r)) lr((overline(t)))$ if either
$(i,j) = (2,-1)$, $(3,2)$, $(3,-2)$ or $i = 4$, $j in {-3,-2,-1,1,2}$. When
$(i,j) = (2,1)$, $(3,1)$, $(3,-1)$ or $(4,3)$, according to
[@bib:l2012-extremal-en-Carter1972],
${r,overline(r),r+overline(r),r+2overline(r)}$ is a class of type $B_2$ and we
set

$
  R_(i j)(t) = x_(overline(r)) lr((overline(t))) x_r lr((t))
  x_(r+overline(r)) lr((t overline(t))) quad (t in K).
$

By [@bib:l2012-extremal-en-Levchuk1990, § @sec:l1990-small-twisted-f4 (I);
@pass:l1990-small-twisted-f4-series[central series table]], $U_k$ in
$U twisted(2, F_4)(K)$ is generated by the elements $R_(i j)(t)$ corresponding
to the columns with number $>= k$ in the following table:

#source(14, printed: 111)
#table(
